       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 5,000 mg three times daily comes to 15 g/day. The usual maximum for a healthy adult is 4 g/day, and many institutions cap it at 3 g/day. A single 5 g dose is also above the normal single-dose limit of 1 g. At this level, the risk of acute liver failure is serious, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **500 mg** by mouth three times daily (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg** by mouth three times daily (about 2 g/day)\n- **1,000 mg** by mouth three times daily (3 g/day)\n- **1,000 mg** by mouth four times daily (4 g/day, the maximum)\n\nIf you really do want 5,000 mg three times daily, tell me the clinical rationale. I would still suggest a pharmacy or toxicology consult first. Let me know the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it."
