       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen at 15 g/day is a toxic dose that could cause serious liver injury or death. It's also more than three times the maximum daily dose, and it wouldn't be safe for this patient whatever their seniority or liver function. Confirming doesn't change the pharmacology.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- Enter a dose within the safe range, such as 1,000 mg by mouth three or four times daily (3\u20134 g/day), or a lower dose if you prefer.\n- Add a note to the order, for example \"max 4 g/24h from all sources.\"\n- If you think the patient needs something beyond standard dosing, you could consult pharmacy or toxicology. I can't enter a dose that would harm them.\n\nIf you meant a different dose, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg, tell me and I'll enter it right away."
